      "content": "That actually helps a lot. So the \"gnawing\" feel is basically just the interaction of those formants and the vocal fold vibration. \n\nI'm also looking at the way these sounds can sometimes sound a bit \"scrappy\" or \"unruly\" in certain contexts—like when the articulation isn't perfectly clean. In acoustics, is there a way to describe these messy, irregular, almost \"cluttering\" sounds that happen when the airflow is disrupted? It's like the sound loses its shape and becomes this weird, irregular, scratchy noise. Is there a technical term for that kind of acoustic \"disorder\" or \"clutter\"?",
